34:| sim findings 2 and 3, as built into the case circuit | Charger enable: R21 pulls the enable line to 3.3 V (not to the charger's REGN pin: its sheet names REGN only as a bias rail, and it would put the module pin above its 3.6 V limit). The case software writes 128 mA (the chip sets the current in 64 mA steps; never above 320 mA), 4.192 V and watchdog off, reads the registers back, then enables. Status light: anode on SYS, R8 510 ohm, R9 and R10 270 ohm (3.0 to 4.6 mA red, 2.2 to 4.7 mA green and blue over 3.5 to 4.35 V). The case software drives the three light pins high at start-up. | `design/ecad/case/sch-notes.md` section 9 (BQ25895 datasheet pages 5, 15, 36, 38, 39; ESP32-S3-MINI-1 sheet page 27; LED sheet page 3). | 2026-11-13 03:15 |
